menuconfig BR2_PACKAGE_AXCL_DRIVER
	bool "axcl PCIe host driver (kernel modules)"
	depends on BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	depends on BR2_aarch64
	help
	  Out-of-tree Axera AXCL PCIe host driver (ax_pcie_host_dev, ax_pcie_msg,
	  ax_pcie_mmb, axcl_host, ax_pcie_p2p_rc) built against the MarkOS
	  kernel. Source: AXERA-TECH's axcl_host aarch64 driver deb (V3.6.2,
	  HF: AXERA-TECH/AXCL) — it ships /usr/src/axcl as a DKMS-style source
	  tree; we drive its kbuild directly with the Buildroot toolchain.

	  Pairing note (int4lab FINDINGS): driver/firmware versions must be
	  compatible with the axclhost runtime; the validated appliance stack
	  is axclhost 3.6.5-m5stack1 + this V3.6.2 driver source + the M5
	  card pac. If a future driver is needed, bump the deb URL + hash.
